 ```
 
+`createPatch(from, to)` computes a JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when applied with
+`applyPatch`, without mutating either argument. The patch only describes what changed: unchanged
+object members and array elements are left out, so a small change does not require resending the
+whole document.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch, applyPatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+const from = { title: 'Hello!', tags: ['a', 'b'] };
+const to = { title: 'Hello!', tags: ['a', 'b', 'c'] };
+createPatch(from, to); // [{ op: 'add', path: '/tags/-', value: 'c' }]
+applyPatch(from, createPatch(from, to)); // deep-equal to `to`
+```
+
 ### JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
 
 `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` applies a [JSON Merge Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7386)
